  "holdout_metric": null,
  "surprise": "732 at 8 loops (seeds 746/765/684) against 502's 690 (687/715/669): +42, the first result in this loop above the spike's 700 bar; keep. The mechanism went as predicted and then some. The fine-tune (level-1 call interval minus its sampling time, which also holds the Lean judge) fell to 51-73 s per round over 579-770 token-budget steps, against about 150 s for the same quantity in 505 (502's RL code on a normal pod), so the fine-tune itself is about 2.5x faster; a round charged to the RL clock fell from about 245 s (502) to 170-195 s on seeds 0/1 and 200-230 s on seed 2, whose weak start sent more targets to retries. 11/11/9 RL rounds fit (502: 7/7/6; predicted 9-10) and RL solved 1265/1264/1208, mean 1246 (502: 1203; predicted 1210-1260). Pretraining is byte-identical: 3338/3443/3461 steps, val at 2 loops 0.0815/0.0868/0.0780. Loops, unchanged by design: metric minus diag +18 (20/22/10; 502: +18, 500: +18); diag 714 (726/743/674; 502: 672), so the whole gain is at both depths and the 8-vs-2 gap did not move. The surprise is where the gain sits. Per-sample dev accuracy barely moved, 0.480/0.483/0.445 at 8 loops (502: 0.466/0.489/0.460) and 0.445/0.445/0.417 at 2 (502: 0.435/0.461/0.436), yet pass@64 rose by 50-60 theorems on seeds 0/1 at every length (seed 0 vs 502 seed 0, lengths 7-13: 112/121/379/100/25/7/2 vs 105/111/360/84/21/5/1), and last-round 1-loop RL acceptance was slightly lower, 0.716/0.703/0.678 (502: 0.730/0.740/0.731; one seed under my 0.70 line, the falsifier needed two). So the extra rounds bought sample diversity, not per-sample accuracy: the 64 attempts cover more theorems at the same hit rate. Candidate causes, not established: more rounds means the found-proof sets are larger and reshuffled into the mix more times (up to 4 distinct proofs per target), and length-homogeneous batches may weight long proofs differently from mixed batches; separating rounds from batching needs a run with the new batching capped at 7 rounds. Round-1 yield predicted nothing again: seed 1 started at 34 targets (1-loop acceptance 0.007) and finished highest at 765. Deeper retries still crack more resistant targets: pooled over seeds and rounds 11.0% at 2 loops, 13.5% at 4, 14.1% at 8 (502: 11.4/13.8/15.9), rounds 3+ 11.5/13.1/13.3. Caveat on the baseline: 502 seed 0's pod sampled at 1 loop at 107-128 samples/s in rounds 2-4 against 220-270 here and 205-237 on 500/503/504/505, so part of 502's 245 s rounds was its pod; the fine-tune comparison above uses 505. 55 patch lines, all in finetune() and token_batches(first=); no crash, pods 68-73 min. Next: a round is now about a third fine-tune, the rest 1-loop sampling and Lean judging, so cheap rounds can be spent deeper (more 8-loop retries, or a second deep pass on targets still resisting after round 6), or the Muon fine-tune the program lists, since the fine-tune now runs 7,000-8,000 steps per run, twice pretraining's.",
